<section class="problem">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-header">

      <div class="section-label">
        The problem
      </div>

      <h2>
        The internet has more information than you need.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Finding information isn't usually the hardest part of learning
        something new. Figuring out what matters, what comes next and
        what you should actually do with it is.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="problem-grid">

      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="number">01</div>
        <h3>Too many resources</h3>
        <p>
          Courses, videos, books, tutorials and articles all compete for
          your attention.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="number">02</div>
        <h3>No clear sequence</h3>
        <p>
          You can find good information and still have no idea what
          should come first.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="number">03</div>
        <h3>Learning without evidence</h3>
        <p>
          Consuming information doesn't automatically create a project,
          portfolio or demonstrable skill.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<!-- SHIFT -->

<section class="shift">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-header">

      <div class="section-label">
        A different approach
      </div>

      <h2>
        Don't collect more information. Build a path.
      </h2>

      <p>
        We organize the learning process around your goal instead of
        handing you another giant list of resources.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="shift-grid">

      <div class="shift-card old">

        <h3>Typical self-directed learning</h3>

        <ul class="shift-list">
          <li>Search for courses</li>
          <li>Save dozens of videos</li>
          <li>Jump between topics</li>
          <li>Wonder whether you're learning the right things</li>
          <li>Finish lessons without producing anything</li>
        </ul>

      </div>


      <div class="shift-card new">

        <h3>Your personalized roadmap</h3>

        <ul class="shift-list">
          <li>Start with a defined outcome</li>
